WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.843
A fictional patient says their fingernails have
changed shape. What would you want to know before
their visit?

2
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:12.900
After installation, create the owner account and
choose Synthetic demo. This case runs on your
computer.

3
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:19.900
Choose the changing fingernails example and answer
the intake questions. So far, we know only the
concern.

4
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:25.702
The patient says the centers dip inward. That
records what they saw. The cause is still unknown.

5
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:33.900
Several nails on both hands. That answer leads to
questions about the timeline and changes in
everyday activity.

6
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:40.900
Watch the other branch. One thumbnail changed last
week. This time the interview asks what happened to
that thumb.

7
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:46.145
Back in the first encounter, the patient says the
shape changed gradually over three months.

8
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:53.378
They now rest halfway up the stairs. That detail
came from the patient when asked about everyday
activity.

9
00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:59.926
They used to climb two flights without stopping.
Now the clinician has a specific change to ask
about.

10
00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:08.725
The patient can keep a nail or eye photo to show a
clinician. The model receives their words. Taking a
photo is optional.

11
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:16.900
At review, the patient adds that they could climb
two flights until last month. Their original
wording stays alongside the correction.

12
00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:24.900
The clinician brief carries the corrected account.
The cause remains open. Verify the findings with a
qualified healthcare professional.

13
00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:30.900
Reopen the saved encounter from the journal. Use a
connected model for an interview about your own
concern.
